---
title: Potato salad
servings: 6
tags: [american, vegetarian, fourth of july, summer, make-ahead]
cuisine: american
time: 1 hour 40 minutes
source: All-American Potato Salad by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/all-american-potato-salad.html
---

Put the @russet potatoes{2%lb}(peeled, cut in 3/4-inch cubes) in a #large pot{} with water to cover by 1 inch. Bring to a boil over high heat.

Add 1 tbsp of the @salt{1%tbsp}, turn the heat to medium and simmer uncovered ~{8%minutes}, stirring once or twice, until a knife slides through with little resistance. Drain.

Tip the potatoes into a #large bowl{}, sprinkle with the @distilled vinegar{2%tbsp} and toss gently. Let them stand ~{20%minutes} until just warm.

In a small bowl, stir together the @celery{1%stalk}(finely chopped, about 1/2 cup), @red onion{2%tbsp}(minced), @sweet relish{3%tbsp}(pickle relish), @mayonnaise{2/3%cup}, @ground mustard{3/4%tsp}, @celery seed{3/4%tsp}, @parsley{2%tbsp}(minced), @ground black pepper{1/4%tsp} and @salt{3/4%tsp}.

Fold the dressing and the @eggs{2}(hard-boiled, peeled, cut in 1/4-inch cubes, optional) gently into the potatoes. Cover and chill ~{1%hour}.

> Dress the potatoes with vinegar while warm so they soak it up. Taste again before serving if it sat overnight.
